think The mechanism: pond/apps/lantern_face_theme.rye imports lantern_face, brush_parse, tokens, and skate_grid, and its resolve_face_theme function runs the real authoring loop -- readFileAlloc under the brush byte bound, parse_brush validating the file, collect_brush_style reassembling the style block, a ThemeMissingMarker refusal when the block names none of the three marker keys, and tokens.resolve infusing the override over the base sheet. The shipped fixture pond/apps/lantern-face.brush authors one token: edge at the warm stone 0xFFB08A5A, so the honest i-don't-know recolors while settled and proposed inherit. Four legs GREEN on the first build: the themed unknown wears the authored stone byte for byte, a themed settled equals the base settled (the cascade leaves siblings alone), the markerless read-source theme refuses by name, and the elder warm-accent fixture -- authored for the mantra browser days ago -- recolors the face's settled through the same loop, one authoring loop serving every face. The witness gains the themed build and three asserts; the whole witness GREEN; TAME clean.
obs The Lantern face v0 family is closed: compose, dress, feed, theme. Every future door -- live completions, multi-row wrap for wider answers, the face inside a real Realidream surface -- belongs to later laps behind their own bookings, and the BUHR equinox gate stands untouched.
